#
# Fixes: erts/configure's chk_arch_ table maps host_cpu names to OTP's
#        ARCH variable. Linux ARM64 reports `uname -m == aarch64`, but
#        OTP < 24 only has entries for armv5b/armv5tel/armv7l/etc. —
#        not aarch64. The catchall sets ARCH=noarch, then the
#        ARCH-$OPSYS case-statement matches `*-darwin*` (or noarch-*)
#        and the build derails downstream.
# Upstream: never landed for old branches. b93b9f9543 ("Update config
#           scripts to compile for Apple Silicon") added arm64 (the
#           Apple Silicon name from `uname -m`) but missed aarch64
#           (the Linux ARM64 name). Both are needed for the awfy
#           workflow which runs measure-linux-target on
#           ubuntu-24.04-arm runners.
# This patch is a pure addition between the existing armv7hl and tile
# entries; both old (no arm64 either) and post-upstream-backport
# (arm64 present, aarch64 still missing) source trees forward-apply
# cleanly because the surrounding context is unchanged.

--- a/erts/configure
+++ b/erts/configure
@@ -6281,6 +6281,7 @@
     armv6hl)	ARCH=arm;;
     armv7l)	ARCH=arm;;
     armv7hl)	ARCH=arm;;
+    aarch64)	ARCH=arm64;;
     tile)	ARCH=tile;;
     e2k)        ARCH=e2k;;
     *)	 	ARCH=noarch;;
